# SRG-APP-000206-WSR-000128  -  CAT II
# A web server utilizing mobile code must meet DoD-defined mobile code
# requirements.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000206-WSR-000128
group:           V-206392
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-001166
control_rev5:    SC-18

contribution:    Splunk Web can restrict the browser-executed content its own pages carry:
                 it sets a Content-Security-Policy that confines dashboard content to the
                 Dashboards Trusted Domains List, warns on redirection to untrusted
                 domains, refuses unsupported hotlinked JavaScript imports, and sends
                 X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN; role design further limits who may author
                 HTML views through the edit_view_html capability.

governs:         web-features.conf - Which features of the web interface are available.
governs:         web.conf - Configures the Splunk Web interface.

check:           web-features.conf [feature:dashboards_csp] enable_dashboards_external_content_restriction not_equals false
check:           web-features.conf [feature:dashboards_csp] enable_dashboards_redirection_restriction not_equals false
check:           web-features.conf [feature:quarantine_files] enable_unsupported_hotlinked_imports not_equals true
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
vendor:          web.conf [settings] x_frame_options_sameorigin https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/web.conf
retired_check:   web.conf [settings] x_frame_options_sameorigin not_equals false
                 reason: "adds a X-Frame-Options header set to 'SAMEORIGIN' to every
                         response served by cherrypy. Default: true". The cookieSameSite
                         entry adds that to embed a dashboard in a third-party iframe "You
                         must also give the 'x_frame_options_sameorigin' setting a value of
                         'false'".
# --- end vendor verification

external:        Determination of mobile code category and the acquisition, development and
                 use policy itself - organizational policy, not a Splunk setting
external:        Digital signing of applets with code-signing certificates - the issuing
                 PKI and the application development process
external:        Mobile code controls on client workstations that download and execute the
                 code - workstation configuration
external:        The contents of the Dashboards Trusted Domains List
                 (dashboards_trusted_domain.<name>) - organization-defined

citation:        web-features.conf.spec:38-46 (enable_unsupported_hotlinked_imports,
                 default false, "CAUTION: Do not change this setting");
                 web-features.conf.spec:50-64
                 (enable_dashboards_external_content_restriction, default true);
                 web-features.conf.spec:66-73 (enable_dashboards_redirection_restriction,
                 default true); web.conf.spec:719-722 (x_frame_options_sameorigin, default
                 true); authorize.conf.spec:730 ([capability::edit_view_html])
finding:         Splunk Web is not configured to the extent the product allows toward the
                 mobile code requirement: one or more of the dashboard external-content
                 restriction, the dashboard redirection restriction, the unsupported
                 hotlinked-import prohibition, or the SAMEORIGIN frame restriction has been
                 set away from its restrictive value.
